Section 124-781(3) conditions for trust interest exchanges:
(a) You acquired the original interest on or after 20 September 1985;
(b) Apart from the roll-over, you would make a capital gain from a CGT event;
(c) You choose the roll-over (jointly with the trustee of the acquiring entity where s 124-782 applies);
(d) If s 124-782 applies, you inform the trustee in writing of the cost base of your original interest.

Section 124-781(4) applies additional arm's length conditions (market value test, same rights and obligations) where the original interest holder and the trustee of the acquiring entity did not deal at arm's length and neither trust had at least 300 beneficiaries.
